          %h2#definition  Definition
          %h3#in_type_theory In type theory
          %p
            We assume a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            with crisp term judgments
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo :
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a::A
            in addition to the usual (cohesive) type and term judgments
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \; \mathrm{type}
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a:A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ξ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi Γ
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ctx
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Xi \vert \Gamma \; \mathrm{ctx}
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ξ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Xi
            is a list of crisp term judgments, and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
            is a list of cohesive term judgments. A crisp type is a type in the context
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ξ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Xi \vert ()
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ()
            is the empty list of cohesive term judgments. In addition, we also assume the dependent type theory has
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/typal+equality"} typal equality
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/judgmental+equality"} judgmental equality
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+cohesion"} axiom of cohesion
          %p
            %em
              There is a crisp type
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ξ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mi R
